&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Growth Marketing Automation Engineer&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location&lt;/strong&gt;: London&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dept&lt;/strong&gt;: Marketing (Growth Marketing)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Weekly office requirement&lt;/strong&gt;: Hybrid, 2 days/week&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Employment type&lt;/strong&gt;: Permanent&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;As our Growth Marketing Automation Engineer you’ll:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Multiply what the whole Growth Marketing team can do. You won’t run a channel or own a campaign, you build the systems, agents and tools that let everyone else operate at a scale they couldn’t reach independently. This is one of the highest-leverage seats on the team. Reporting to the VP Growth Marketing this role is deliberately team-agnostic, sits across Growth Marketing and collaborates with the entire marketing team. You are the glue and the force-multiplier between them.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll be doing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Set the build roadmap. &lt;/strong&gt;Work with VP Growth Marketing and other stakeholders to agree a quarterly roadmap of the highest-leverage builds. You’ll have a clear backlog and the air cover to say no to the rest.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Find and automate repetitive work. &lt;/strong&gt;Find the repetitive tasks eating the team’s time and replace them with agents and automations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Act as a force multiplier across the team. &lt;/strong&gt;Build systems that increase the impact of high-leverage work. Examples include: multiply our ABX operations; use GWI’s MCP and API to generate personalised content at scale; Connect data sources and context to create a Growth Marketing OS that surfaces what’s working, what isn’t, and what we should do next.Find growth levers in the funnel and fix/scale. Run analysis and discovery to discover the biggest levers and run experiments to improve conversion or unlock new growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What do I need to bring with me?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing campaigns, channels and funnels. You know how they work and know how to run a test. You could be a growth or performance marketer who has gone all-in on AI and wants it to be the main part of your job.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are a problem-solver and builder by default. You welcome messy, open-ended problems&amp;nbsp; and are relentlessly curious and resourceful.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You build with AI, not just chat with it: chaining prompts, wiring up agents, and automating work.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data literacy and a systems thinker: you can think through problems end-to-end, document a clear scope and create a structured plan that links back to a measurable outcome.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You don’t need a computer science degree or a software engineering background, but you’re comfortable in low/no-code platforms, happy wiring up APIs and MCP, and you pick new tools up fast.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus points for:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
