&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;Who we are&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Typeform is a refreshingly different form builder. We help over 150,000 businesses collect the data they need with forms, surveys, and quizzes that people enjoy. Designed to look striking and feel effortless to fill out, Typeform drives 500 million responses every year—and integrates with essential tools like Slack, Zapier, and Hubspot.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;About Typeform&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Typeform helps people create better conversations at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Millions of people use Typeform to collect information, understand their customers, generate leads, run research, gather feedback, and power workflows across their businesses.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are continuing to evolve Typeform from a form builder into a broader platform for collecting, understanding, and acting on information. AI is becoming a major part of that direction, both through experiences we build for customers and through making Typeform easier for AI agents and other products to interact with.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Senior Product Manager to help shape what comes next.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;The role&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Product Manager at Typeform, you will own a meaningful product area and work closely with Engineering, Design, Data, Research, Marketing, and other teams to turn customer problems and business opportunities into products people genuinely want to use.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will be responsible for understanding the problem space, setting product direction, deciding where the team should focus, and helping the team move from insight to execution.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is not a role where Product simply writes requirements and hands them to Engineering.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We expect our Product Managers to be close to customers, opinionated about the problems worth solving, comfortable making decisions with incomplete information, and able to bring teams together around a clear direction.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will balance customer value, product quality, technical considerations, and commercial impact while helping the team move quickly and learn.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What you will do&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the strategy and roadmap for a key area of the Typeform product.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a strong understanding of our customers, their workflows, and the problems they are trying to solve.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities through customer conversations, behavioural data, research, market insight, and product intuition.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn broad problems into clear product bets, hypotheses, and measurable outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Design and Engineering from discovery through delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Data and Research to understand customer behaviour and evaluate whether what we build is working.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make thoughtful prioritisation decisions across customer needs, business goals, technical investment, and product quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define success measures and use them to guide product decisions before and after launch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run experiments where appropriate and use the results to shape future product direction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Marketing, Sales, Customer Success, and other teams to ensure we understand the wider customer and commercial context.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate product direction clearly and build alignment across teams and leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help teams move from ideas to shipped experiences without losing sight of the original customer problem.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Look beyond individual features and think about how your product area contributes to the wider Typeform platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Explore how AI can improve the customer experience, change existing workflows, and create new ways for customers to get value from Typeform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What we are looking for&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have significant experience building and scaling digital products, ideally within SaaS, product led growth, collaboration software, productivity tools, or another strong product environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable taking on messy, ambiguous product problems and bringing structure and direction to them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong focus on customer problems and outcomes, rather than jumping straight to features.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong product judgement, with the ability to use customer insight, data, and context to make good decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Close collaboration with Engineering and Design, with product development treated as a shared discipline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to set a clear product direction while staying practical about what the team should focus on next.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Confident making trade offs, making decisions, and explaining the thinking behind them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good judgement around when to experiment, when to research, and when there is enough evidence to move forward.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear communication, with the ability to adapt complex ideas for different audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commercial awareness and an understanding of how product decisions can influence activation, engagement, retention, expansion, and revenue.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Curiosity about AI and how it is changing the way products are built and how customers interact with software.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A real care for product quality and the details that shape a strong customer experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;You might be particularly strong in one or more of these areas&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We do not expect every Senior Product Manager to have the same background.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Depending on the team, relevant experience could include:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Product led growth, onboarding, activation, or retention&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Creation tools, editors, builders, or content creation experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Platform products, APIs, integrations, or developer ecosystems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analytics, insights, research, or data products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pricing, packaging, payments, or monetisation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI powered products, agents, automation, or intelligent workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;B2B SaaS products used across multiple teams and use cases&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;*Typeform drives hundreds of millions of interactions each year, enabling conversational, human-centered experiences across the globe. We &lt;strong&gt;move as one team&lt;/strong&gt;, empowering our collective efforts by valuing each individual’s unique perspective. This fosters &lt;strong&gt;strong bonds&lt;/strong&gt; grounded in respect, transparency, and trust. We &lt;strong&gt;champion our diverse customer base&lt;/strong&gt; by anticipating their needs and addressing their challenges with priority. Committed to excellence, we&lt;strong&gt; hold high expectations &lt;/strong&gt;for ourselves and each other, continuously striving to deliver exceptional results.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are proud to be an equal-opportunity employer. We celebrate diversity and stand firmly against discrimination and harassment of any kind—whether based on race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity or expression, or veteran status. Everyone is welcome here.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Makes Cloudbeds Unique&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;At Cloudbeds, we&#39;re not just building software, we’re transforming hospitality. Our intelligently designed platform powers properties across 150 countries, processing billions in bookings annually. From independent properties to hotel groups, we help hoteliers transform operations and uplevel their commercial strategy through a unified platform that integrates with hundreds of partners. And we do it with a completely remote team. Imagine working alongside global innovators to build AI-powered solutions that solve hoteliers&#39; biggest challenges. Since our founding in 2012, we&#39;ve become the World&#39;s Best Hotel PMS Solutions Provider and landed on Deloitte&#39;s Technology Fast 500 again in 2024, but we&#39;re just getting started.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location: &lt;/strong&gt;Remote (Europe)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How You&#39;ll Make an Impact:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a &lt;strong&gt;Staff Software Engineer&lt;/strong&gt; in Revenue Intelligence, you will shape the technical direction of systems that help hospitality businesses understand demand, identify revenue opportunities, and make better pricing and commercial decisions. You will work across customer-facing applications, backend services, data pipelines, analytical stores, recommendation workflows, and cloud infrastructure. This is a hands-on leadership role: you will solve complex engineering problems directly while establishing architecture, improving reliability and security, reducing systemic technical debt, and aligning multiple teams around durable technical decisions. Your impact will extend beyond individual features to the quality, scalability, operability, and long-term evolution of the Revenue Intelligence platform.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Revenue Intelligence Team:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Revenue Intelligence team builds products and platforms that turn hospitality data into practical decisions for hoteliers, including pricing recommendations, demand insights, reporting, automation, and commercial opportunities. Our systems span frontend experiences, APIs, distributed services, data processing, machine-learning workflows, and production infrastructure. We value pragmatic engineering, strong ownership, evidence-based decisions, and technical leaders who raise the effectiveness of the people and systems around them.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Bring to the Team:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set and evolve the technical strategy for Revenue Intelligence, translating product and business goals into coherent architecture and executable engineering plans&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the design and delivery of complex capabilities across customer-facing web applications, backend APIs, event-driven services, data pipelines, analytical storage, and recommendation workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and resolve systemic risks in scalability, reliability, security, data quality, observability, and operability before they become recurring customer or engineering problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive modernization of legacy systems and infrastructure through incremental, well-reasoned migrations that preserve delivery momentum and production stability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product, Data Science, Infrastructure, Security, and engineering leaders to define boundaries, contracts, ownership, and long-term platform direction&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Remain hands-on in the codebase through implementation, technical spikes, design reviews, debugging, incident response, and the most consequential or ambiguous engineering work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Raise the technical effectiveness of the wider organization through mentoring, architecture guidance, engineering standards, documentation, and constructive challenge&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Sets You Up for Success:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of software engineering experience, including significant technical leadership across complex production systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep hands-on expertise in Python, with the ability to work effectively across both ecosystems and guide engineering decisions beyond a single language&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong architecture and distributed-systems fundamentals, including API design, event-driven workflows, consistency, failure handling, scalability, and service boundaries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with data-intensive systems such as PostgreSQL, Redshift or similar analytical platforms, batch and streaming pipelines, and large-scale data processing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing or operating recommendation systems, machine-learning platforms, pricing systems, experimentation workflows, or other decision-support products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong cloud and platform engineering experience across AWS, containers, Kubernetes, Terraform, Helm, Argo CD, CI/CD, observability, and secure production operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A demonstrated ability to lead through influence, create alignment across teams, communicate complex tradeoffs clearly, and drive decisions from ambiguity to execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong record of improving engineering quality through testing strategy, operational readiness, incident learning, security, documentation, and sustainable technical standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Product judgment and customer empathy, with the ability to connect technical investments to measurable outcomes for hoteliers and the business&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Business-level English fluency and experience collaborating effectively in a remote, globally distributed organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Skills to Stand Out:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep hands-on expertise in .NET/C#&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What to Expect - Your Journey with Us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Behind Cloudbeds&#39; revolutionary technology is a team of redefining what&#39;s possible in hospitality. We&#39;re 650+ employees across 40+ countries, bringing together elite engineers, AI architects, world-class designers, and hospitality veterans to solve challenges others haven&#39;t dared to tackle. Our diverse team speaks 30+ languages, but we all share one language: a passion for innovation and travel. From pioneering breakthroughs in machine learning to revolutionizing how hotels operate, we&#39;re not just watching the future of hospitality unfold – we&#39;re coding it, designing it, writing it, and shipping it. If you&#39;re ready to work alongside some of the brightest minds in tech who are obsessed with using AI to transform a trillion-dollar industry, this is your chance to be part of something extraordinary.&lt;/p&gt;
